# Muxiz Full-Stack Music Platform Architecture & Guidelines

## 1. Core Architecture
- **Mobile (Flutter)**:
  - State: `flutter_riverpod` (StateNotifierProvider, NotifierProvider)
  - Audio Engine: `just_audio` + `audio_service` with single `ConcatenatingAudioSource`
  - Audio Routes: Native Platform Channel (`com.muxiz.app/audio_route`)
  - Local Storage: `shared_preferences` / `local_storage.dart` for JWT tokens, cache, offline tracks
  - Network: `dio` with automatic JWT Bearer token interceptor (`api_client.dart`)
- **Backend (NestJS)**:
  - Database: PostgreSQL with Prisma ORM
  - Auth: JWT auth (`JwtAuthGuard`) + zero-friction Guest session generation (`/auth/guest`)
  - Endpoints: `/songs`, `/playlists`, `/users`, `/favorites`, `/search`, `/recommendations`

## 2. Audio Pipeline & Queue Rules
- Never create duplicate `AudioPlayer` instances.
- Never use unbound delays or microtask loops to append playlist sources; use direct single-pass `AudioSourceManager.createPlaylist()`.
- Synchronize all queue insertions (`playNext`, `addToQueue`, `reorderQueue`) simultaneously across `QueueManager`, `MuxizAudioHandler`, and `just_audio`.
- Honor `AudioRepeatMode` (off, all, one) and queue boundaries on next/previous track skips.

## 3. UI/UX & Design Standards
- Premium Spotify & Apple Music inspired aesthetic: Dark background (`#121212`), high contrast, vibrant dominant color extraction from album artwork.
- Optimistic UI updates with instant user feedback for Likes, Playlists, and Downloads.
- Floating Mini Player with smooth gestures (tap to expand, swipe horizontal for next/previous).
- Hardware audio device picker with live battery indicator and native AirPlay/Bluetooth system routing.

